it <i>this easy</i> to point to the original way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-05-2017, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T09:53:02-08:00","id":1058449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058431#post1058431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's how Temporal Sympathy works...</div> </div> </div> </div>From my understanding, you would need to actually had some relic from Nakatomi to cast Postcognition on, not just a random antique from the Edo period. Or somehow go full Dr. Who/Back to the Future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:07:43-08:00","id":1058457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058449#post1058449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From my understanding, you would need to actually had some relic from Nakatomi to cast Postcognition on, not just a random antique from the Edo period. Or somehow go full Dr. Who/Back to the Future.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why? Cannot you cast on the period item Space Scrying to look around it and 'teleport' your view point to proper Edo across space distance when seeing in the past?<br /> <br /> Remember, we <i>do not</i> look for the Nakatomi herself by this method - we just look over Emperor Palace, where Edo Consilium surely would be. But looking over 'footage material' we surely would found mages that would have contact with local Hierarch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:16:23-08:00","id":1058459,"title":"","content":"You don't need a relic. Just cast poscognition on the area with a current picture of the place. You don't get the bonuses for a good sympathy, but you pronably won't need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:19:09-08:00","id":1058461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058443#post1058443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No problem - just find me <b>one</b> original katana or armor from the period - it does not need to be from Edo / Tokyo area even, just age of it is important. I assume that at least one item from 500 years before survive to modern era in some private Sleepers collection in whole Japan. If not, mages of Mysterium would keep sustaining at least one in Atheneum with Time or Matter magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This I can see in the setting - I just point that obfuscating this whole Nakatomi thing should took large portion of factions day-to-day routine then, as it <i>this easy</i> to point to the original way.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Any object that is from that era would get you easy scrying access to whoever had that item, and not much else. Trying to see Nakatomi from a scry of a farmers hoe or something like that is not impossible, but you'd basically have to wrench far and hard away from your base point. It also probably doesn't help you if Nakatomi has preventative measures against being scryed up at the time-and paranoia about attacks from the future or past are serious things in the setting.<br /> <br /> 2) It's also worth noting that Nakatomi is just an icon to modern mages outside of her Mystery-people use her to argue their political stances much like Jesus has been used to argue for every sort of political situation under the sun. If modern mages found out what she was really like, they'd probably ignore it and just keep on keeping on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:21:11-08:00","id":1058463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058457#post1058457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">we just look over Emperor Palace, where Edo Consilium surely would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Emperor lived in Kyoto at this point.<br /> <br /> Also, a palace seems like a really bad location for your secret society; I doubt the Shogun rents the palace for functions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:28:01-08:00","id":1058467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058463#post1058463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Emperor lived in Kyoto at this point.<br /> <br /> Also, a palace seems like a really bad location for your secret society; I doubt the Shogun rents the palace for functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the Consilium meeting place that is surely one of the places mages are most paranoid about seems like a really bad place to try and magically intrude on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:54:39-08:00","id":1058476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058467#post1058467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the Consilium meeting place that is surely one of the places mages are most paranoid about seems like a really bad place to try and magically intrude on.</div> </div> </div> </div>They still go to the meetings. You do not have have to spy into Consilium meeting place - just look over it's entrance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:57:51-08:00","id":1058477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058457#post1058457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? Cannot you cast on the period item Space Scrying to look around it and 'teleport' your view point to proper Edo across space distance when seeing in the past?</div> </div> </div> </div>How you even can, if Temporal Sympathy can only be used on Time spells that call for it and other spells Combined with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:59:55-08:00","id":1058479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058476#post1058476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They still go to the meetings. You do not have have to spy into Consilium meeting place - just look over it's entrance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>1) They can still see you.<br /> 2) They can still smack you.<br /> 3) They will probably still be warded against you.<br /> 4) Do you even know what Nakatomi looks like?<br /> 5) Also, you assume they leave through the door.<br /> <br /> Remember Cornelius's lament: &quot;The trouble is, the other side can do magic too, Prime Minister.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:18:12-08:00","id":1058489,"title":"","content":"Going for a place where you have a good reason to belive Nakatomi actually walked by is very different than casting on any random antique and hoping to get lucky. in that scenario, the place where Nakatomi passed by is in itself a relic: it was in direct contact with him at some point of it's history. Although what you would learn just from that wouldn't be very useful. Can you nest Postcognitions on top of one another? I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:29:24-08:00","id":1058495,"title":"","content":"Probably some hella potent magics protecting against such things, which is part of the mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:04:13-08:00","id":1058560,"title":"","content":"Doesn't a spell utilizing Temporal Sympathy have to be cast on the subject as it is now? And isn't the period when Nakatomi - assuming they even existed - was in the area completely unknown? So wandering to some random stretch of Tokyo, even assuming it <i>was</i> somewhere of note when the place was old Edo, and just casting Postcognition to look back is, to put it mildly, a doomed effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:22:37-08:00","id":1058571,"title":"","content":"Magic makes things easy, but it doesn't make things trivial. <br /> <br /> Such has always been the world mages live in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:35:16-08:00","id":1058576,"title":"","content":"I don't have Imperial Mysteries so I can't say this with much certainty, but my understanding is that if Nakatomi did Ascend then Time and Sympathy spells would not find her as reality now believes she never existed. Your only hope would be to find something that slipped through the cracks, a personal relic that would still have sympathy with her, and at this point I would point out that the one group likely to have such relics are the Mysterium, which also happens to be the group with the most to lose if her secrets came out.<br /> \u200bThe core book does say that the Mysterium can't devote much of its efforts to pure research because they are kept busy defending their control of the Tokyo Consillium.<br /> \u200bMaybe what is keeping them so busy is finding and securing any evidence of Nakatomi's real life. Finding out that she was a woman who ran a Kabuki theater is not something those in power would be proud of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:37:46-08:00","id":1058579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058560#post1058560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't a spell utilizing Temporal Sympathy have to be cast on the subject as it is now? And isn't the period when Nakatomi - assuming they even existed - was in the area completely unknown? So wandering to some random stretch of Tokyo, even assuming it <i>was</i> somewhere of note when the place was old Edo, and just casting Postcognition to look back is, to put it mildly, a doomed effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be noted that the root of this conversation comes from the Fallen Blossoms Dark Era, where in Nakatomi is basically shown to definitively exist as just a mage. To some people's minds, this means she should be instantly scryable, and questions surrounding her are moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:09:52-08:00","id":1058596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058579#post1058579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted that the root of this conversation comes from the Fallen Blossoms Dark Era, where in Nakatomi is basically shown to definitively exist as just a mage. To some people's minds, this means she should be instantly scryable, and questions surrounding her are moot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a Nakatomi is shown to definitely exist as a Mage in Edo. That doesn't mean she is the same person as the mythical Nakatomi. What David said about Inoue Akio applies here too:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1056740-fallen-blossoms-in-print?p=1057782#post1057782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could be a complete coincidence<br /> <br /> Could be a relative with the same name<br /> <br /> Could be the same [person]<br /> <br /> The name could be a magical power, who gets stolen by new people<br /> <br /> Could just be an homage<br /> <br /> Could technically be two different names. The way kanji work, you could have thirty different people with the same sounding name, who all have technically different names because of the various readings<br /> <br /> That's just a few off the top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that Edo's Nakatomi chose that as her Shadow Name either as tribute or to try and manipulate the power of the name. In the same way that a Viking Mage using the name Ivar Vidfamne or Beowulf doesn't make them the legendary kings, a Japanese Mage using the name Hakatomi doesn't have to be the truth behind the legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:19:26-08:00","id":1058603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058560#post1058560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't a spell utilizing Temporal Sympathy have to be cast on the subject as it is now? And isn't the period when Nakatomi - assuming they even existed - was in the area completely unknown? So wandering to some random stretch of Tokyo, even assuming it <i>was</i> somewhere of note when the place was old Edo, and just casting Postcognition to look back is, to put it mildly, a doomed effort.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But what if you use Fate magic to wander (at random) into a place where such postcognition is possible and then, again at random, pick exactly the moment you are looking for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:26:06-08:00","id":1058606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058603#post1058603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But what if you use Fate magic to wander (at random) into a place where such postcognition is possible and then, again at random, pick exactly the moment you are looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that even possible with Fate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:32:29-08:00","id":1058609,"title":"","content":"Lucky Number yourself some GPS coordinates and Lucky Number yourself some, em, time coordinates. Or do a smart casting of Shifting the Odds. Or do some works with Strings of Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:28:04-08:00","id":1058639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058603#post1058603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what if you use Fate magic to wander (at random) into a place where such postcognition is possible and then, again at random, pick exactly the moment you are looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, theoretically, some combination of words that would drive a Tetrarch to tears and make them forsake their gods. Should an Acanthus be able to randomly flick back and forth through a dictionary until they speak a sentence that causes an Archmaster to repent of their wicked ways? There is, theoretically, some combination of events and occurrences that should cause a Sleeper to become a Sleepwalker or even Awaken, so why haven't Acanthus thearchs Awakened the whole world yet?<br /> <br /> There's different levels of probability and likelihood. Fate might guide you into a series of events that brings you to the conclusion, but it rarely lets you choose how you get there. &quot;Get me temporal sympathy to Nakatomi&quot; might see you ending up trying to steal an ancient book from a Yakuza drug lord, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:37:32-08:00","id":1058648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058596#post1058596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a Nakatomi is shown to definitely exist as a Mage in Edo. That doesn't mean she is the same person as the mythical Nakatomi. What David said about Inoue Akio applies here too:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It could be that Edo's Nakatomi chose that as her Shadow Name either as tribute or to try and manipulate the power of the name. In the same way that a Viking Mage using the name Ivar Vidfamne or Beowulf doesn't make them the legendary kings, a Japanese Mage using the name Hakatomi doesn't have to be the truth behind the legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that could be true.<br /> <br /> I don't think it actually is, but it could be true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:52:39-08:00","id":1058655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058648#post1058648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, that could be true.<br /> <br /> I don't think it actually is, but it could be true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I whole heartedly agree. I'm just pointing out that there can be perfectly mundane explanation in addition to the supernatural ones. Either of which means the mystery is still a mystery.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Rereading the Mage Tokyo chapter, it explicitly says no one has been able to use Time to observe Nakatomi or the charter she created. So I bet this trick wouldn't work. Personally, I'm sticking with my temporal dead zone hypothesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 03-05-2017, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T12:32:28-08:00","id":1059121,"title":"","content":"We don't have enough background information to really speculate but I could see the truth of the Tokyo mystery of Nakatomi turning out to be a Mysterium creation, that they are actively hiding the truth for political reasons. It would be a major diversion from their core purpose and doomed to blow up in their faces, but it would make for a good chronicle with lots of tension.<br /> The real mystery then would be why did they do it and when did they start?<br /> <br /> \u200bOne relatively simple idea on this would be that a Kabuki theater running Nakatomi (if this is the same Nakatomi) became involved with the Baijin and the Shogun's war on the supernatural. After the fall of the shogunate and the beginning of the Meiji Restoration any ties to the Shogun and some of his secretive actions might not have been palatable to new Awakened or involved secrets that the Mysterium (possibly with the support of the Guardians) decided should remain secrets for few were ready to know them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 03-06-2017, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:19:23-08:00","id":1059156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1059121#post1059121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't have enough background information to really speculate but I could see the truth of the Tokyo mystery of Nakatomi turning out to be a Mysterium creation, that they are actively hiding the truth for political reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>There seems to be an implication that that's at least partially true. It's interesting that the charter of Nakatomi that the dominant faction follows forbids women from being on the consilium and refers to Nakatomi as a man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The real mystery then would be why did they do it and when did they start? </div> </div> </div>2e core has this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...all physical rolls and meeting notes from Nakatomi\u2019s original Consilium were destroyed in the 1657 Great Fire of Meireki </div> </div> </div>The wording implies that Nakatomi is already gone by then, plus the section refers to Nakatomi as among the first magi that any records cover and that the records go back 500 years, which would be about 140 years before Fallen Blossoms which is the 1640s. Even a thyrsus would be pushing their luck at that age.<br /> <br /> Now I think about it, it is kinda interesting that the legendary mage vanishes from history around the same time as a cataclysmic fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T16:46:08-08:00","id":1059271,"title":"","content":"Okay, scratch that. Beast mentions Nakatomi being around at the end of the 19th century. So there seems to be a few hundred years that have been edited out or something...<br /> <br /> Interestingly, despite being at least 300 years old that Nakatomi wasn't the Apex of Edo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T17:02:18-08:00","id":1059276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1059271#post1059271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, scratch that. Beast mentions Nakatomi being around at the end of the 19th century. So there seems to be a few hundred years that have been edited out or something...<br /> <br /> Interestingly, despite being at least 300 years old that Nakatomi wasn't the Apex of Edo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you were right the first time. Same name (although without the Kanji we can't be sure), different person. Same deal with the Edo Nakatomi. She has a definite gender and lives a significant amount of time after the mythical Nakatomi, whose gender is unknown (if they existed). That or the sorceress that was in the Great Kami's court was the original Nakatomi... who is an archmage. Talking, inspiring, those things are okay for her. Actually using magic to interfere would be another story. It would fit with the epic nature of Kami's court for them to be somewhat engaged with the Ascension War though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T17:53:07-08:00","id":1059289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1059276#post1059276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you were right the first time. Same name (although without the Kanji we can't be sure), different person. Same deal with the Edo Nakatomi. She has a definite gender and lives a significant amount of time after the mythical Nakatomi, whose gender is unknown (if they existed). That or the sorceress that was in the Great Kami's court was the original Nakatomi... who is an archmage. Talking, inspiring, those things are okay for her. Actually using magic to interfere would be another story. It would fit with the epic nature of Kami's court for them to be somewhat engaged with the Ascension War though.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, it'd be the same kanji, \u4e2d\u81e3.<br /> <br /> This was an exceedingly common name in antiquity, since it was a powerful family. The human family didn't really have much prominence in either of the eras being discussed here, but were immensely influential between the sixth century AD and the twelfth. But having two influential characters named Nakatomi wouldn't even seem an off coincidence. Whether or not they're related or the same person, that's a whole different question. The classical Nakatomi could be completely, 100% forgotten and that wouldn't even remotely erase the name from prominence, because it's so ubiquitous. Further, most modern family names are very modern, dating back no further than the 19th century. Which adds some complexity to the issue. <br /> <br /> This is doubly important to note: Through a significant part of Japanese history, most people didn't really have two names. Most people had a single name, and identified by a place of birth or origin. Nakatomi could be such a signifier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T17:57:17-08:00","id":1059292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1059289#post1059289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this case, it'd be the same kanji, \u4e2d\u81e3.<br /> <br /> This was an exceedingly common name in antiquity, since it was a powerful family. The human family didn't really have much prominence in either of the eras being discussed here, but were immensely influential between the sixth century AD and the twelfth. But having two influential characters named Nakatomi wouldn't even seem an off coincidence. Whether or not they're related or the same person, that's a whole different question. The classical Nakatomi could be completely, 100% forgotten and that wouldn't even remotely erase the name from prominence, because it's so ubiquitous. Further, most modern family names are very modern, dating back no further than the 19th century. Which adds some complexity to the issue. <br /> <br /> This is doubly important to note: Through a significant part of Japanese history, most people didn't really have two names. Most people had a single name, and identified by a place of birth or origin. Nakatomi could be such a signifier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I had suspected some of that, but that adds another level of complexity to the question. Thanks David!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T18:07:10-08:00","id":1059293,"title":"","content":"The whole Nakatomi issue is beginning to become a really captivating Mystery regarding names and sympathies. A potential gold mine for Mastigos, and anyone delving into the Space Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T21:09:27-08:00","id":1059334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1059293#post1059293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole Nakatomi issue is beginning to become a really captivating Mystery regarding names and sympathies. A potential gold mine for Mastigos, and anyone delving into the Space Arcanum.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Time - I'm still not convinced why Time mage in Edo area just cannot burrow Sympathies and look into proper periods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T23:25:47-08:00","id":1059364,"title":"","content":"Second Chances noted in a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1058655#post1058655\">previous post </a>that at least in the case of Nakatomi, something flat-out blocks temporal observation of that period. Which means that what we have here is not an answer to a Mystery, but a new Mystery - a typical turn of events for mages in the field.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Even without that, I assume you're wondering why Postcognition (+ Temporal Sympathy) + Scrying won't get you seeing Nakatomi. I've done some thoughts about why this is a herculean task, and compiled my reasoning. (Note how I'm not saying it's an absolutely impossible task)<br /> <br /> Spoiler tags because it's long, and largely just a compilation of what myself and others already said before.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> First, a relic connected to Nakatomi.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does it even exist? As posters before me pointed out, disasters that wipe out entire towns were common back then. And no, please refrain from the old &quot;But mages have magic and can prevent the disaster or salvage the valubles!&quot; argument. Mages are still people, and people are fallible. Mistakes, oversights, and changes in priority happen. And I highly doubt mages in the past bothered to magically maintain their leader's possessions just so the future generation could peer through them, when they have other Mysteries at hand to chase and are paranoid of future mages meddling with their timeline.</li> <li>Is it authentic? The Shroud of Turin was supposedly the burial shroud of Jesus, but look how that one turned out.</li> <li>Was personally in contact for meaningful amount of time with Nakatomi? This condition is required for Scrying to actually work. If the relic is an object, the mage can follow it around to get a view. Even then, since the window is focused on the relic itself, actual sight of Nakatomi and their surroundings might not be much visible. And unless you hit the jackpot and acquired Nakatomi's dedicated tool or something of similar personal importance, chances are they didn't always carry it on their person. There will be blank spots in time where Nakatomi just left that object alone, leaving the scrying window staring at the object and not its owner. If the relic is a site, then it had better be somewhere Nakatomi personally resided and discussed topics of importance to the present day mages, since the scrying window only gives a static overview of the location.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>No, the Sympathetic Range Attainment will not allow the Scrying window leave the relic and follow Nakatomi around. Sympathetic range is applied to the distance between the mage and his Scrying spell's subject, which in this situation is the relic, not Nakatomi. Sympathetic range will be only good for letting you do this task from the safety of your sanctum, so other mages don't find you snooping around the relics.</li> </ol></li> <li>Does the sympathy remain? Sympathies come and go naturally, and it is entirely possible that the relic has changed so much that its temporal sympathy to its days in Edo is even below Weak level.</li> </ol>Second, mages of the past.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Is that Nakatomi they're seeing the real deal? The above posts give a good reason that the Nakatomi seen by mages may not be the 'real' Nakatomi. From common family names to Shadow Names to identical kanji pronunciations.</li> <li>Why would they let you spy on them? Mentioned above, but mentioning it once again. Mages don't like other mages spying on them, whether they're from the future or not. That goes the same for mages in the past; they have no reason to just let present mages spy on them, and will put up decoys and defenses.</li> <li>What about the temporal anomaly? What Second Chances pointed out as existing. May not be the work of mages at all, but listing it here since it's still a problem in the past.</li> </ol>Third, your peer mages in the present.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Who has vested interests? The Mysterium and its ruling faction, of course. It's entirely possible that they pooled their resources to go over all of what I just described above and saw the truth behind Nakatomi... and decided to bury it for one reason or another.</li> <li>How will you convince everyone? Okay, so you went through all hardships above and obtained the truth. Great. And now the ruling mages publicly decry you as a forger and a heretic. You now must play in a House of Cards, where a single misstep will kill your political standing.</li> </ol></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If the player character cabal triumphs despite all that (and it <i>will </i>be the player characters, not anyone else, since they're the ones with enough initiative and talent to do so, and are under the aegis of &quot;Storyteller approval&quot;), then they have every right to take credit for and bask in the glory of having unraveled what may have been the biggest Mystery hidden in Tokyo's history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T15:23:44-07:00","id":1062021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058424-2e-power-of-sympathies-or-how-you-cannot-forget-nakatomi?p=1059334#post1059334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And Time - I'm still not convinced why Time mage in Edo area just cannot burrow Sympathies and look into proper periods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't suppose that Nakatomi could actually have been a powerful Acanthus, or at least powerfully skilled in Time magic, and habitually warded everything that would conclusively prove his/her activities? Combine with cleaning of sympathetic/temporal connections for the purposes of security, and then loosing Consilium records in the centuries to come from one disaster or another, it isn't that hard to imagine that the truth has slipped beyond the grasp of most mages.<br /> <br /> Also, the areas where you want to scry may now be an Ansho, a dead magic zone. This would make looking back impossible unless you solved the Ansho Mystery first...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T15:30:46-07:00","id":1062024,"title":"","content":"Mages can temporally ward themselves, and they would be wise indeed to use them. Last thing a mage needs is to be flanked from the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}